description:
FOUND s513f (Opus, 2026-10-09) while building #2874 (`use bigrat` is ANNOUNCED instead of built because of this). Probe scratch/s513f/pr/bf1.pl in the s513f worktree:
    use Math::BigRat; my $r = Math::BigRat->new("1/3"); print $r + Math::BigRat->new("1/6"), "\n"; print Math::BigRat->new("3/4") * 2, "\n";
perl 5.40.3: 1/2 / 3/2.  PCL (s513f tree): 2 / dies "Unhandled sb-int:simple-program-error" (an arity error inside a transpiled core-module sub -- not tidy, not perl's).  Math::BigInt and Math::BigFloat answer the same shapes correctly (bigint/bignum shims work).  When it runs, lib/bigrat.pm becomes the same three lines as lib/bignum.pm (overload::constant integer/float/binary => \&NAME with Math::BigRat->new).
